      "id": "yeats-collected-poems-s0394-p00834",
      "source_en": "(page 56)\nThis poem is founded on an old Gaelic ballad that was sung and translated for\nme by a woman at Ballisodare in County Sligo; but in the ballad the husband\nfound the keeners keening his wife when he got to his house. - 18gg.",
